<script type="text/javascript">
    // Joyce's first figure: the three given angles drawn as the isosceles
    // triangles ABC, DEF, GHK (AB, BC, DE, EF, GH, HK equal), the triangle
    // LMN on AC, DF, GK, its circumcircle with centre O and radii OL, OM,
    // ON, and the points P, Q of the second reductio.
    //
    // Added, hidden at rest: solid twins of the arms (BAs .. HKs) so the
    // given angles stand before AC, DF, GK are joined, and LOs, MOs, NOs so
